  "Question": "A bug crawls along a number line, starting at \\(-2.\\) It crawls to \\(-6,\\) then turns around and crawls to \\(5.\\) How many units does the bug crawl altogether?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(9\\)",
    "B": "\\(11\\)",
    "C": "\\(13\\)",
    "D": "\\(14\\)",
    "E": "\\(15\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The total distance includes both legs of the journey. From \\(-2\\) to \\(-6\\), the bug crawls \\(6-2=4\\) units. It then crawls \\(6\\) units from \\(-6\\) to \\(0\\), followed by \\(5\\) more units to reach \\(5\\). Therefore it crawls\n\\[\n4+6+5=\\boxed{15}\n\\]\nunits altogether, choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
